body:
@mkinney Could you clarify the intended feature-control boundary before further implementation? The bounded probe and exact remaining paths are in my previous result: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3191#issuecomment-7207646884 .

Target-side native dev controls aligned eight dependency feature sets, but the selected lower-library units still differ through host proc-macro `syn` features and the standalone post/UI `rustix` OS/network feature union. No complete fix or PR exists.

Is a test-build-only solution that explicitly aligns those remaining host and native OS/network feature sets acceptable, provided normal/wasm builds and kernel `truck` isolation remain unchanged? Or should those separate variants be retained and the single-library acceptance refined? I recommend settling that boundary before another broad batch; I will not change grouped-build/fallback behavior or widen production dependency features without an agreed design.
